1
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:18,460
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:23,580
kick a pebble and let
it fly until it's gone.

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:29,320
To the Kashiwa type who
was always joking around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,840
they laughed at me for
staying as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:38,740
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,
it's all just serious business.

6
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:43,920
One nightmare,
but the unchanging streets are kinder still.

7
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:48,900
The crows are cawing,
so the day is already ending.

8
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,900
Can you really see the yakitori?

9
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:11,180
Thank you for watching.

10
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:31,640
Nice weather

11
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:34,540
On a day like this,
I've got no motivation to work

12
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:41,400
You're certainly early today, Ryotsu.

13
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:43,260
Chief.

14
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:47,680
You're early too, Chief.

15
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:49,360
Do you know what time it is?

16
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:54,320
I told you yesterday and the day before to come in on time,
didn't I?

17
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,678
Well this is I wonder why,

18
00:01:56,728 --> 00:01:59,940
I don't know why,
but how did it end up like this?

19
00:01:59,940 --> 00:02:02,888
I guess it must be my everyday behavior,
or something.

20
00:02:02,938 --> 00:02:06,080
In other words,
maybe the chief's teaching of me was wrong?

21
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:08,560
Bakabōn!

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,580
Goodbye, Operation Ryo-san!

23
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,480
How many times do you have to
be late before you're satisfied?!

24
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:21,280
Just quit your job already!

25
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,380
N-no way...

26
00:02:22,380 --> 00:02:24,720
When I think someone like
you is my subordinate,

27
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:26,500
I'm so ashamed I could cry.

28
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:27,760
You're not crying, though.

29
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,480
It's a figure of speech!

30
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:32,860
Forget it.

31
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:34,560
Hurry up and get to work.

32
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,320
Yes, sir.

33
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:38,120
Geez, you're noisy every single day.

34
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:40,460
Senpai...

35
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,240
That's my seat, you know.

36
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:43,840
W-what?

37
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:45,120
Senpai's seat is...

38
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:48,220
It's been moved over there.

39
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:53,500
What?! What is the meaning of this?

40
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:58,140
The chief said people who don't
work don't need a desk, so...

41
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:00,360
Got a problem with that, Ryotsu?

42
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:06,960
No, well, I'm going to work, work, work!

43
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,380
Hey, Reiko!

44
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:16,020
What?

45
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:19,340
I'm working! Don't disturb my work!

46
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:24,100
Working?
You were just doodling, weren't you?

47
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,100
Hey!

48
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:29,180
Come on, you're in the way, move, move.

49
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:36,660
I'm back! I finally got the taiyaki from Sankakuya,
the one everyone says is delicious!

50
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,940
You actually managed to get it?

51
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:41,960
I waited in line quite a while.
Here you go, Chief.

52
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:42,940
Thanks.

53
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:44,600
Reiko, you too.

54
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:45,180
Thank you.

55
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:48,660
Here you go, Nakagawa.

56
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:49,480
Thanks.

57
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,300
And this one is mine.

58
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,120
Why?

59
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:53,200
My share?

60
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:58,280
Why is there no taiyaki for me?

61
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,060
Sorry, Ryo-san.

62
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:01,040
I completely forgot.

63
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:03,160
Have you been treating me
like a nuisance all along?

64
00:04:04,820 --> 00:04:06,480
Knock it off, you idiot!

65
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:08,600
It's just taiyaki,
so don't go on grumbling about it.

66
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,300
I haven't had any either, Ryo-chan.

67
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,200
"It's just taiyaki," you say?

68
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,076
Well, everyone else got to eat,
so it's fine.

69
00:04:16,126 --> 00:04:18,260
But I'm the only one who didn't get to eat.

70
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,360
Honestly, you're acting like a child.

71
00:04:21,560 --> 00:04:25,494
Enough already!
You can't even do your job properly, and

72
00:04:25,544 --> 00:04:27,118
all you care about is stuffing your face.

73
00:04:27,168 --> 00:04:30,120
A person like that doesn't need any taiyaki.

74
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:32,746
There's no need to say that much, is there?

75
00:04:32,796 --> 00:04:35,120
You could at least show
me a little more respect.

76
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,576
Don't be ridiculous.
If it were only that you can't work,

77
00:04:37,626 --> 00:04:40,100
at least you wouldn't keep
causing trouble time after time.

78
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:42,880
Why on earth should I
respect a guy like that?!

79
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:45,620
Nobody would be troubled if you disappeared!

80
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:48,360
Actually, this police box is
more peaceful when he's not here!

81
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,700
Got it, you big idiot!

82
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:57,720
What a character he was...

83
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,800
Look, it's all Ryotsu-related!

84
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,240
Get out of the way!

85
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:03,560
Get off the bridge!

86
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:06,900
I can walk wherever I want, can't I!

87
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,680
What a guy!

88
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:11,980
He's like common sense's worst nightmare,
a walking lack of decency.

89
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:13,600
Just you wait.

90
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:14,720
What?

91
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:29,300
Shame him!

92
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:30,200
Expose him!

93
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:32,120
Just get lost, you!

94
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,940
How dare you pull this crap on us!

95
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:36,120
You'll regret this!

96
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:38,580
Please go home.

97
00:05:39,140 --> 00:05:41,020
We, the Shopping District Federation,

98
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:43,160
have decided that Ryo-san

99
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:45,600
is not to sell anything,
as decided at our last regular meeting.

100
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,380
What?

101
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,800
Sales have been falling lately,

102
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:49,900
and everyone's having a tough time.

103
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,420
At a time like this, as usual,

104
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,600
we can't stand having goods taken on credit.

105
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,920
I haven't even

106
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,880
Anyway, your unpaid tabs up until now

107
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,380
unless you pay them all back,

108
00:05:58,380 --> 00:05:59,900
we can't sell you anything.

109
00:05:59,900 --> 00:06:00,440
No way.

110
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:02,620
Go home, go home!

111
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,220
Damn it, even those guys...

112
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,340
Honda.

113
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:11,780
What's wrong?

114
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:14,340
Look, we're busy right now.

115
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:18,480
Damn it, even that Honda guy...

116
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:24,660
This stupid dog!

117
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:36,140
Damn it!
Even the crows are making a fool of me!

118
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:46,940
Damn it! Everyone treats me like a nuisance!

119
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:56,160
Ryo-san really is a handful, isn't he.

120
00:06:56,160 --> 00:07:00,760
Exactly! I told him yesterday, and he's
surely going to be late again today.

121
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:03,300
Hm?

122
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:04,620
Ryotsu!

123
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:08,620
Yoisho, there.

124
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:11,620
Phew.

125
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:14,820
Yes!

126
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:18,103
I wonder what's gotten into him,

127
00:07:18,153 --> 00:07:20,820
Senpai? Suddenly so serious?

128
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:23,380
Maybe what happened
yesterday really got to him.

129
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:25,800
Is it because I forgot to buy the taiyaki?

130
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:29,000
Hmph, it won't last three days.

131
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,060
Here you go.

132
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:31,620
All of your accumulated tabs?

133
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:36,000
I figured I'd at least pay off
the model shop's share for now.

134
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,340
Check it.

135
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:41,000
Sure enough,

136
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,160
Just give the others a little more time.

137
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:45,520
I'll definitely pay on my next payday.

138
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:48,520
I'm really sorry for
everything up until now.

139
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:53,920
The patrol results: nothing unusual.

140
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:57,120
If you're looking for the community center,
go straight down this road

141
00:07:58,940 --> 00:08:00,580
Ryo-chan, this case

142
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:01,660
I already took care of it.

143
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:06,800
Excuse me, aren't you going home yet?

144
00:08:06,980 --> 00:08:09,240
I want to finish this report today,

145
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,280
Here...

146
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:17,320
Chief, Officer Ryotsu and
I are heading out on patrol.

147
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:25,800
It's been two weeks now, you know.

148
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,040
What on earth has happened to him?

149
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:30,560
Is it because I forgot to buy the taiyaki?

150
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:35,100
Senpai, what's gotten into you, really?

151
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:35,940
What?

152
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:39,880
You've been so serious lately,
like a different person.

153
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:40,740
Throws you off, does it?

154
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:43,880
No, not at all... but what on earth

155
00:08:43,880 --> 00:08:48,780
Well, I've got various reasons...
various things, you know.

156
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:51,460
Various things?

157
00:08:52,520 --> 00:08:53,380
Senpai.

158
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:58,660
I bought takoyaki.
Would you like some, Senpai?

159
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:01,240
Well? Honda?

160
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:03,240
W-what's gotten into you?

161
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:04,900
Everything's all tidied up.

162
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:07,360
Doesn't it look like you're moving out?

163
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:10,360
Is it so strange for me to clean my room?

164
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,500
No, no, I didn't mean that -

165
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,400
Right.

166
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,300
Honda, I'll give you this.

167
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:15,541
This is -

168
00:09:15,591 --> 00:09:18,360
Isn't this a Shin-Buto helmet?!

169
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:20,240
You said you wanted it before, didn't you?

170
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,260
R-really? Is it really okay?

171
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:25,260
Yeah, I've got to sort
out some of my things.

172
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:27,580
A departing bird leaves no mess behind,
as they say.

173
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:28,400
What is it?

174
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:31,100
No, nothing, nothing.

175
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:32,440
Oh?

176
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,020
Chief Ohara

177
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,720
We have something to ask you.

178
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:45,060
Is it true that Kankichi
Ryotsu is quitting this station?

179
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:46,120
What?

180
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:50,780
Apparently, Chief Ohara demoted Ryotsu
and sent him to that far-off police box.

181
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:53,120
No, I don't know!
I don't know anything about it!

182
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,780
Then what's going on?

183
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:57,500
The whole station is buzzing
with that rumor right now.

184
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,420
W-well, even if you say that...

185
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:03,260
Excuse me.

186
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:08,760
Perfect timing.
I was just about to talk about Ryotsu.

187
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:11,120
I wanted to ask you about it too.

188
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:15,020
There's a rumor going around that
Ryotsu is leaving the station,

189
00:10:15,020 --> 00:10:17,300
what exactly is going on with that?

190
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,140
Y-yes...

191
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:20,560
Actually,
I don't know anything about it either.

192
00:10:20,560 --> 00:10:23,100
That's why we came to see you, Chief.

193
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:29,520
Lately,
Ryotsu has been working oddly seriously.

194
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:32,600
Isn't there some connection between the two?

195
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:34,600
Well, I couldn't say.

196
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:38,580
Yes, but it's gone flying, though.

197
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:41,300
It's the Police Commissioner-General.

198
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:45,320
Yes, I'm honored.

199
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:47,900
Ryotsu, Kankichi.

200
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:48,707
Yes,

201
00:10:48,757 --> 00:10:52,360
Ryotsu is indeed stationed here,

202
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,880
what has he done?

203
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:57,820
Kankichi Ryotsu, Senior Constable, is
ordered to transfer from Katsushika Station.

204
00:10:57,820 --> 00:10:59,680
Ryotsu is being transferred.

205
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:08,460
Ryo-chan's being transferred?

206
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:11,980
Yes, the Police Commissioner-General
personally called me.

207
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,600
Apparently it was decided
about two weeks ago.

208
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:20,220
It seems Ryotsu's extraordinary energy and
stamina caught the attention of headquarters.

209
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:23,400
Then, could it be that
Ryo-san knew about this?

210
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:27,240
Yes. It seems it was discussed
unofficially beforehand.

211
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:27,880
So,

212
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:32,040
Senpai, you were thinking things through in your own way,
weren't you?

213
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:34,680
But you didn't have to keep it from us too.

214
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:37,600
Well, anyway,
it's a promotion to Headquarters.

215
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,080
This time, let's send him off properly.

216
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:41,320
Yes.

217
00:11:44,100 --> 00:11:48,040
Senior Constable Kankichi Ryotsu,
reporting back from patrol.

218
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:51,080
All clear throughout the jurisdiction.

219
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,040
Good work.

220
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,300
Yes, sir!

221
00:11:58,740 --> 00:11:59,380
What?

222
00:12:00,820 --> 00:12:01,900
No, well, it's nothing.

223
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:04,980
Senpai, congratulations on
your promotion to headquarters.

224
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:06,140
Congratulations, Ryo-chan.

225
00:12:06,140 --> 00:12:08,360
Congratulations, Ryo-san.

226
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:11,580
So you found out

227
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:14,620
Come on, that's cold.
Why didn't you tell us?

228
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,380
It was hard to bring up.

229
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:20,860
I've always caused nothing
but trouble at this station,

230
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:23,140
and I've given everyone so much grief.

231
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:25,960
So when I heard I was leaving,

232
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:30,040
I couldn't help thinking
everyone might be glad.

233
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:34,160
But it's all right now.

234
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:37,640
After all,
everyone brought this on themselves.

235
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,660
Chief Ohara, and everyone else too.

236
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:46,040
I only have a few more days left at this Kameari Kōen-mae Hashutsujo,
Translation>
so

237
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:48,440
until then, please take care of me.

238
00:12:49,280 --> 00:12:52,640
Ryo-san,
I hear you're leaving the Katsushika station

239
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:53,900
That's right.

240
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:56,000
But don't worry about it.

241
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,280
I'll pay everyone back
what I owe before I go, so.

242
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:00,920
No, it's fine, Ryo-san.

243
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:03,120
We talked it over with everyone,

244
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,860
and to celebrate Ryo-san's
promotion to headquarters,

245
00:13:05,860 --> 00:13:08,340
we've decided to wipe out your debts.

246
00:13:08,340 --> 00:13:11,340
You've looked after us in so many ways.

247
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:15,020
You're the best customer on the whole shopping street,
so to speak.

248
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:17,100
So the other day's money, this too,

249
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:19,360
put it toward your moving
expenses or something.

250
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:21,760
No, no, that's too much.

251
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:24,340
Don't mention it. Come on, just take it.

252
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:26,740
Right, but that's one
thing and this is another.

253
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,100
It's fine, it's fine.

254
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,600
Hey, what about my desk?

255
00:13:30,600 --> 00:13:33,120
Senpai, please use this one.

256
00:13:33,740 --> 00:13:34,660
Is that really all right?

257
00:13:35,860 --> 00:13:37,600
Since the Chief has given his permission,

258
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:41,420
you've only got a little
while left at this police box.

259
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:44,820
Finish up your remaining work at that desk.

260
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,620
Thank you, Chief Ohara.

261
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:51,480
I'll do my very best in my new post.

262
00:13:53,900 --> 00:13:56,080
This seat really is the most comfortable.

263
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,880
Ryo-san, I'm sorry about the other day.

264
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,400
I bought taiyaki from Sankakuya.

265
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:07,200
If you'd been transferred
without eating that taiyaki,

266
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:09,160
I'd have regretted it
for the rest of my life.

267
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,640
Don't exaggerate.

268
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,280
Come on, Ryo-san, just try it.

269
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:18,000
Well then,
I'll take you up on that and eat it.

270
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:19,980
How is it?

271
00:14:21,060 --> 00:14:22,880
It's really delicious, Jerai.

272
00:14:22,880 --> 00:14:23,540
I'm glad.

273
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:28,680
Thanks, Reiko. Thank you, Reiko.

274
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:36,820
As expected,
the tea Reiko makes is the best.

275
00:14:44,060 --> 00:14:44,720
Ryotsu

276
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,380
Yes.

277
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:48,180
Make sure you do your
best at headquarters too.

278
00:14:48,180 --> 00:14:48,660
Yes.

279
00:14:48,660 --> 00:14:52,040
I've always been hard
on you about everything.

280
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:55,760
But all of that was only because
I wanted what's best for you.

281
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:56,740
I know.

282
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:58,860
Honestly, I've been a lucky man.

283
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:01,620
Getting to work under
someone like you, Chief.

284
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:06,420
Everything I am today is thanks to you, Chief.
I will never forget your kindness.

285
